    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Places, people and study habits",
     "texto": [
      "Today we talk about school, university and how people study.\n\n- **The system:** after the ESO there are two years of **bachillerato** and then university.\n- **At university:** you **te matriculas** (enrol) at the **secretaría**. The **catedrático** is the most senior teacher and each student has a **tutor**. With an **intercambio** you study abroad and with **prácticas** you work in a company.\n- **Classes:** a **conferencia** is a talk by a guest. Careful: a *lectura* is a text to read.\n- **To study:** you take **apuntes**, **subrayas** the important parts, make an **esquema** and a **resumen**, and **repasas** before the exam.\n- **When there are problems:** «Tengo una duda», «Me he **equivocado**». The teacher **corrige** the exams."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Verbs with e → i",
     "texto": [
      "Verbs in **-ir** such as **corregir**, **repetir**, **pedir**, **elegir** and **seguir** change the **e** of the stem into **i** when that syllable carries the stress:\n\n- **corregir** → corrijo, corriges, corrige, corregimos, corregís, corrigen\n- **repetir** → repito, repites, repite, repetimos, repetís, repiten\n\nIn **nosotros** and **vosotros** the **e** does not change.\n\nWith **corregir** and **elegir** there is one more change in spelling: before **o** the **g** becomes **j** (**corrijo**, **elijo**) to keep the sound.\n\nVerbs in **-ar** and **-er** do not make this change."
     ],
